---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import AvatarBanner from '../assets/avatar-banner.png';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet"
	pubDate={new Date('July 24 2026')}
	heroImage={AvatarBanner}
>
	<p>
		Hello 👋 I'm Josh, but better known on the internet by my monicour, Sewdohe. I'm a long-time hobby developer and Linux user. FOSS advocate. Mechanic by day
		and developer by night (mostly on weekends lol). I've been responsible for some pretty cool projects, but nothing huge. I'm a piddler, really.
	</p>
	<p>
		At 12 I wrote my first ugly little html page. I can still remember the horrible brushed metal background with red text - but something about being able to
		breathe life into a browser using simple text was magical for me. I was hooked. Ever since then I've had a deep love for creating things on the computer. After my first
		couple simple webpages I began learning design - I would participate in "signature competitions" on various fourms...one of which I remember vividly was the Gameshark forums.
		What a strange place that was. Odd to even think about an "active forum" these days - the internet has changed so much since I was younger. I wish I still had the things 
		I made from that era - I used to upload everything to a place called photobucket. It's a long gone website now - along with everything I used to design.
	</p>
	<p>
		In my current era, I mostly just piddle on weekends. My 9-7 job is as a mechanic. While I'm able to do things to cars I never thought I'd be able to do, 
		I violently wish I could work full-time as a developer. Sadly, life must come first. As a father to two children I have to do what pays the bills. Turn wrench. Maybe
		one day I can break the poverty-cycle and get a better job that would free up my time to focus on becoming a developer, but for now...I just piddle on what I enjoy on the weekends
		while a turn wrench during the weekdays.
	</p>
</Layout>
